(Another) one of the ideas from #nethack ideas collection #7 gets
implemented - this one makes it so that under a certain condition your
character is "innumerate" - they cannot count the quantities of items.
The numerical values for stacks of objects ("12 appples") are replaced
with quantifying adjectives ("several apples").

Currently, the criteria for innumeracy is "Int < 8". I have some
reservations about this, but I can't think of anything more
appropriate.

CAVEATS:
* Your gold counter will still show your exact worth, even though coins
will appear as "lots of coins" in your inventory.
* You currently cannot wish for "some", "several", "many", "lots of",
"hundreds of" and "thousands of" a certain item. Maybe a little later.

And the patch is at http://www.greyfire.org/~l/innumeracy.diff

P.S: I think I might have heard of a similar thing existing in ADOM,
but it could have just been an unimplemented RFE of someone's.
